BEGIN_DESC
TANTRA BETA 11 - Moon, charging station and energy cells (demo).
The MPU's battery is four energy cells, 250 kWh / 80 kg each, in bays in its RIGHT side between the middle axles (red handles).
Its power socket is on the front bumper (right). The station 12 m ahead of it: a cabinet with a 15 m cable on a reel, a rack of
six cells, 300 kW input. The MPU starts low: its cells at 35, 40, 20 % and one bay empty.
CHARGING: at the station's front F - take the cable; walk to the MPU's front bumper (the cable trails after you) - F plugs it in.
Charging runs at up to 300 kW, the emptiest cell first (the socket's hint shows the charge and the power). F at the socket - the
plug back into your hands; F at the station - the cable back on its reel. Walk or drive farther than 15 m - the plug pulls out.
CELLS: F at a cell's hatch on the MPU's right side - the cell out into your hands; F at the station's rack - put it on charge, or
take a charged one; F at an empty bay of the MPU - put it in. One thing in the hands at a time. 80 kg weighs 13 kg here.
Driving: walk up to the platform, F climbs on; F at the post; W/S/A/D, Shift, Space emergency brake, B parking brake.
END_DESC

